      "id": "ss9xywe",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1.1 Definition of Computer"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Computers are defined by their fundamental operational functions and key characteristics.",
        "Computers are classified based on technology into Analog, Digital, and Hybrid types.",
        "The history and development of computing are categorized into distinct Generations of Computers.",
        "Understanding foundational computer concepts is essential for competitive exam preparation."
      ],
      "id": "sw6xxux"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1g7rikn",
      "content": "A computer is an electronic device that takes raw data as input, processes it using programs, stores the data, and produces output in the form of information."
    },
    {
